{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.He4TwoRowDominance","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.He4TwoRowDominance","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.BraidKnot.TwoRowStratum","lean:module:QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCapDerived"],"declarations":27,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_eq_nine_three_in_stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_eq_nine_three_in_stratum","kind":"theorem","line":183,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L183-L190","doc":"Concrete consequence: the dominant block (9, 3) is in Λ²(12)\neven when stated using the explicit witness value rather than\nthe class-field abstraction. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_ne_trivial_rep","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_ne_trivial_rep","kind":"theorem","line":174,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L174-L181","doc":"The leading non-trivial block is not the trivial representation.  Derived\nfrom `leading_ne_largest` and `largest_eq`, so it holds for any instance\nrather than being read off this one. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.largest_in_two_row_stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.largest_in_two_row_stratum","kind":"def","line":165,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L165-L172","doc":"The largest block overall also lies in Λ²(12).  It is the trivial\nrepresentation `[12]`, a ONE-row partition — `IsTwoRow` is `length ≤ 2`,\nso Λ²(12) contains it, which is why the stratum ratio is exactly 1 with\nthe trivial block included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_in_two_row_stratum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.dominant_in_two_row_stratum","kind":"def","line":157,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L157-L163","doc":"The dominant block (9, 3) belongs to the two-row stratum\nΛ²(12).  Composes `dominant_is_two_row` and `dominant_sums_to_12`\nvia `twoRow_of_length_le_two`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_complement_at_most_20_percent","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_complement_at_most_20_percent","kind":"theorem","line":149,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L149-L155","doc":"The complement (non-two-row) contribution is at most 20% of\n`|tr_M(β_⁴He)|`.  Direct corollary of `ratio_lower_bound`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_complement_eq_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_complement_eq_zero","kind":"theorem","line":142,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L142-L147","doc":"Under convention D (`ratio = 1`), the non-two-row complement share is\nidentically `0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.instHasHe4DominantBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.instHasHe4DominantBlock","kind":"instance","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L124-L135","doc":"Empirical instance pinning the leading non-trivial block to `(9, 3)` and the\noverall largest block to `(12)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.instHasHe4TwoRowDominance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.instHasHe4TwoRowDominance","kind":"instance","line":114,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L114-L122","doc":"Canonical convention-D instance for ⁴He: `ratio := 1` unconditionally\n(matching both `he4_twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl` and the 50-dps witness\n`he4-canonical-tr-m-block-fingerprint.witness.json`, and retiring the\nsuperseded convention-C `866/1000` numeral; `bean qou-58w3`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.leading_ne_largest","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.leading_ne_largest","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L112-L112","doc":"**The two are different**, and that is the content of this class.\nBefore the 2026-09-05 intra-nucleon ordering ruling the two notions\npicked out the same block, so one field expressed both and nothing\nrecorded which was meant.  Under the canonical ordering the trivial\nrepresentation `[12]` leads at 85.4 % against `(9,3)`'s 64.4 % —\nnot because it rose (its character is a product of per-letter\nscalars and no reordering can move it) but because every other block\nfell past it.  It leads in six of the eight atoms tabulated, so it\nis not a fingerprint of ⁴He; `(9,3)` is.  Carrying both, and\nasserting they differ, is what keeps the distinction visible. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_eq","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The empirical value: the trivial representation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_sums_to_12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_sums_to_12","kind":"theorem","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L99-L99","doc":"It sums to 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_is_two_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_is_two_row","kind":"theorem","line":97,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L97-L97","doc":"It is two-row (a one-row partition has length 1 ≤ 2). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.largest_partition","kind":"def","line":95,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L95-L95","doc":"The largest block by `|c_λ|` OVERALL, trivial representation included. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_eq","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_eq","kind":"theorem","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L93-L93","doc":"The empirical value. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_sums_to_12","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_sums_to_12","kind":"theorem","line":91,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L91-L91","doc":"It sums to 12. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_is_two_row","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_is_two_row","kind":"theorem","line":89,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L89-L89","doc":"It is two-row. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_partition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.dominant_partition","kind":"def","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The leading NON-TRIVIAL block: the largest `|c_λ|` among the blocks\nwhose character is not fixed by construction.  This is the quantity\nthe magic-shell reading refers to. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock.mk","kind":"ctor","line":83,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L83-L83","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4DominantBlock","kind":"class","line":80,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L80-L112","doc":"The dominant non-trivial block λ* for ⁴He is `(9, 3)`, while the largest\nblock overall (including the trivial representation) is `(12)`.  Empirically\nverified at 50 dps in `he4-canonical-tr-m-block-fingerprint.witness.json`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_upper_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_upper_bound","kind":"theorem","line":78,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L78-L78","doc":"Upper bound: at most 100 % (corollary of `ratio_eq_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_lower_bound","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_lower_bound","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L76-L76","doc":"Lower bound: at least 80 % (corollary of `ratio_eq_one`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_eq_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio_eq_one","kind":"theorem","line":74,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L74-L74","doc":"Exact convention-D support: the two-row stratum carries the full trace. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.ratio","kind":"def","line":72,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L72-L72","doc":"The two-row stratum's share of the trace (`1` under convention D). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance.mk","kind":"ctor","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L70-L70","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.HasHe4TwoRowDominance","kind":"class","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L64-L78","doc":"The two-row stratum's share of `tr_M(β_⁴He)` under canonical convention D.\nBecause convention D (`z_D = q³/(q²+1)`, Wenzl level `r = 2`) kills every\npartition with `ℓ(λ) > 2` identically (`he4_twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl`),\nthe two-row share is `ratio = 1` unconditionally (`ratio_eq_one`), which a\nfortiori satisfies the `4/5 ≤ ratio ≤ 1` bounds consumed by downstream\npropositions (`bean qou-58w3`). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:he4-two-row-dominance","label":"prop:he4-two-row-dominance","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L53-L62","doc":"The two-row stratum share of a nonzero ⁴He Wedderburn trace sum is\nunconditionally `1` under convention D (`r = 2`), specializing\n`QOU.MassTheory.TwoRowCap.twoRow_share_eq_one_of_wenzl`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_threeRowPart_eq_zero_of_wenzl","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidKnot.He4TwoRowDominance.he4_threeRowPart_eq_zero_of_wenzl","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/he4-two-row-dominance.lean#L45-L51","doc":"The `≥ 3`-row complement of the ⁴He Wedderburn trace sum vanishes identically\nunder convention D (`r = 2`), by `threeRowPart_eq_zero_of_wenzl`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}